        <p>It is stated that some 1,5076 children are suffering from measlea at Northampton, and that all the Board schools and most of the other public elementary schools are closed.</p>
        <p>The Unique "revised version "of the Bible which was adopted on Saturday by the Board of Eduration of I Chicago for the use of schools has been in preparation some years. It contains only two prayers—one being the Lord's Prayer, which is set to music. The 23rd Psalm also finds a place in it. The Song of Solomon is omitted entirely ; so also are the stories of Abraham and Sarah. The Psalms have been greatly cut, so that only terse extracts appear. The story of Jos?ph has been treated in serial form, each adventure beim: narrated in a separate chapter. The revised Bible opens with the thirtieth and thirty-first verses of the twelfth chapter of the Gospel according to St. Mark, followed by the tenth chapter of the same gospel. Then come the Proverbs and the Book of Job and the ether selected passages. The whole volume consists only of 200 pages of large print.</p>
