      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-02-22_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>POLICE REPORT.</head>
        <p>POLICE REPORT.</p>
        <p>The report of the police as to the cause and com- mencement of the fire is to the effect that at .5.40 a.m. Benjamin Hickson, foreman carter at the Central Station,observed that a fire had broken out, in the top spinning room of the mill. He at once ran into Winwick-street and gave information to P.C,'s Wood and Delahay who proceeded to the market and rang the fire.bell. On getting the sum- mons,Superintendent Turner and his staff proceeded to the scene of the outbreak with two steam en- gines, and commenced to throw water on the build- ing. They confined the fire to the one storey which was completely burnt out, the roof haying fallen in. The fire was originated by the lighting of a gas at one of the machines by a workman named Joseph Garnett. The " fluff " ignited and the fire spread rapidly along the room.</p>
