        <p>DR. J. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE, THE ORIGINAL AND ONLY GENUINE. CIILORODYNE is admitted by the Profession to be the most wonderful and valuable remedy ever dis- covered. CHLORODYNE is the best remedy known for Coughs, Consumption, Bronchitis. and Asthma. 011LORUDYNE effectually checks and arrests tho ie too often fatal diseases.—Diphtherla, Fever, Croup, Ague. CHLORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhoea and is the only specific in cholera and Dysentery. CHLORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy Hysteria, Palpitation, and Spasms. piILORuDYNE is the only palliative in Neural- gia, Rheumatism, Gout. Cancer, Toothache, Menin- gitis, &amp;c. From Dr. B. 3. POULTON and Co., Horncastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne in Our practice lately, and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ. and from whatever cause. It induces a feeling of comfort and quietude not obtainable by any other remedy, and it seems to possess this great advantage over all others sedatives; that it leaves no unpleasant after effects. " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from her Majesty's Consul at Manilla, to the effect that Cholera had been raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CHLORO- DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December. 1864. CAUTION.—BB WARE OF PIRACY AND IMI- TATIONS. CauTtoN.—Vice Chancellor Sir W. PAGE WOOD stated that Dr. J. Comm BROWNE was, undoubtedly, the inventor of "CHLORODYNE " and that the story of the defendant FREEMAN, was d..liberately untrue, which he regretted to say, had beeu sworn to.—See Times, 13th July, 1864. Sold in bottles at Is. 10., 2s. 9d., and 4s. 6d. None is genuine without the words " DR. 3. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLGRODYNE" on the Government Stamp. Overwhelm- ing Medical testimony accompanies each bottle. SOLE MANUFACTURER.—J. T. DAVENPORT, 33, Great Russell st., Bloomsbury, London.