        <p>LYMM. SUBSCRIPTION Brass BAND.—Gn Monday. the first annual ball was held in connection with the above hand. and was a decided success, a goodly number of young men and women joining in twirling the light fantastic toe to the strains of Mr. T. T. Gregson's Qqadrille Band. The room was artistically decorated, and the refresh- ments provided by Mrs. McCready, of the Church Hotel, were entirely satisfactory. The dance came to an end about 2.30. a.m.</p>
